# `engines` is advisory without this — pnpm warns and installs anyway, which is
# how `"node": ">=20"` sat in package.json as a claim nothing tested. Measured
# 2026-09-13 on Node 20.17.0: six of the wallet's 45 spec files never load
# (ERR_REQUIRE_ESM through jsdom), only 554 of 648 tests run at all, and
# `digits.test.ts` fails `expected '١٦:٣٠' to be '16:30'` — non-negotiable #12.
# So >=22 is a correction, and this line is what makes it bite.
engine-strict=true
